# Byte-exact generated artifacts.
#
# data/boundary-collection.json records `geometrySha256`, the sha256 of the raw
# bytes of the generated GeoJSON. scripts/validate-boundaries.mjs and
# packages/domain/test/boundaries.test.mjs re-hash the working-tree file and
# compare. Git must therefore never rewrite these files' line endings on
# checkout: with core.autocrlf=true on Windows the single trailing LF is
# checked out as CRLF, which changes the file by one byte and breaks the
# comparison even though the content is intact.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion, so the working-tree bytes stay
# identical to the committed blob on every platform. The committed blobs are
# already LF, so this adds no renormalisation and no content change.
#
# A checksum mismatch here means the artifact or its pin really changed.
# Regenerate with scripts/import-boundaries.py; never edit the expected
# checksum, the generated GeoJSON or the metadata by hand to make a test pass.
apps/web/public/data/*.geojson -text
